  "description": {
   "en": "\"Nino Kuni\" is a place where spirits and gods live. Anyone who wanders into it cannot return alive.\n\nWhen Nagi was little, he would always say \"Good morning\" to the big sister at the shrine. He didn't even know her name, but he looked forward to seeing her every day. But then, her big sister suddenly disappeared. Even now that he's grown up, whenever he passes by the shrine he remembers those days and wishes to see her again. That's when he hears a voice saying \"Good morning.\" Where's my big sister?! Nagi frantically searches for the shrine. He suddenly finds himself standing on a staircase with an invisible torii gate leading to it... \"Where am I?!\" Nagi tries to turn back, but is unable to return to the exit.\n\nA strange sight then appears, accompanied by the sound of drums. A group of people wearing strange masks are dancing to music, and among them is a particularly beautiful shrine maiden.",
   "ja": "物の怪と神が住む「弐の国」、迷い込んだ人間は生きて帰ることはできない。\n\n小さい頃【おはよう】といつも挨拶を交わしていた神社のおねえちゃん。\n名前も知らないけど、薙は毎日会えることが楽しみだったーー。\nでもーーおねえちゃんは突然いなくなってしまった。\n\n成長しても神社を通るたびにあの頃を思い出し、また会いたいと願う。\nそんな時に聞こえた「おはよう」の声ーー。\nおねえちゃん!?と薙は神社を夢中で探す。\n\n気が付くと先の見えない鳥居が続く階段に立っていた…「どこだ、此処!?」\n薙は一度引き返そうとするも出口に戻ることができないーー。"
  },
